# API access: tokens for programs that may read the device inventory (e.g. opensecmon).

nav-api-tokens = API access
api-tokens-subtitle = Tokens for programs that may read the device inventory, for example opensecmon. A token only allows reading the name, address and system description of the devices.
api-tokens-none = No token yet
api-tokens-none-hint = Create a token below. The other program sends it with every request.
api-token-name = Name
api-token-name-hint = What the token is for, for example “opensecmon”.
api-token-created = Created
api-token-last-used = Last used
api-token-never-used = never
api-token-create = Create token
api-token-new = New token “{ $name }”
api-token-shown-once = The token is shown only now. Copy it and enter it in the other program; it cannot be looked at later. If it is lost, revoke it and create a new one.
api-token-revoke = Revoke
api-token-revoke-confirm = Really revoke
api-token-revoke-hint = Programs using this token get no answer afterwards.
api-token-name-invalid = The name must be 1 to 64 characters long and must not contain control characters.
api-token-name-taken = A token with this name already exists.
api-tokens-usage = How a program reads the inventory
flash-api-token-revoked = Token revoked.
